## CI policy (DND-2.3+)

```text
feature → develop
= local Sprint Final Quality Gate only (no GitHub CI required)

develop → master
= GitHub promote-gate + quality verification (required)
+ mandatory local full Playwright matrix (Chromium/Firefox/WebKit) before develop push

FX.6 established: GitHub does not reinstall browsers or rerun the 108-test matrix on promotion.
      Dispatch CI manually to run browser-e2e on GitHub.
```

Do not pull into active work unless the sprint explicitly requires it:

- Phase 3 Auto-Layout work outside a dedicated follow-up sprint
- Phase 4 production changes outside an authorized follow-up (Phase 4 is COMPLETE AND SHIPPED in `0.1.0-alpha.4`; no Alpha.5 / Phase 5 without a separate explicit planning gate)
- Beta readiness work outside the currently authorized BETA-0.x sprint (Beta release remains NOT AUTHORIZED)
- Flutter implementation (separate track; Core-contract dependent)
- Vue (DND-FX.2 COMPLETE — do not reopen unless authorized), Angular (DND-FX.3 COMPLETE — do not reopen unless authorized), Svelte (DND-FX.4 COMPLETE — do not reopen unless authorized; do not add `@dndgem/sveltekit`)

